Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# eslint output
eslint-output.txt

# Emitted TypeScript declarations.
# Reason: 57 of these plus their source maps were committed by accident in Feb 2026,
# went stale immediately, and were mistaken for a third copy of the models that had to
# be kept in step with database/ and apps/admin/database/. They never were: TypeScript
# resolves the sibling .ts first, so they were inert. Deleted 1 Sep 2026 after proving
# removal left the typecheck byte-identical (16 errors main, 225 admin, before and after).
# tsconfig is noEmit, so nothing regenerates them - these rules only stop a stray
# `tsc -d` run putting them back.
# The same applies to the compiled .js beside each .ts, and those were worse than inert:
# vitest resolved the stale .js in preference to the .ts, which made all 57 modules -
# every model plus the money-critical services - unimportable in tests.
#
# Note the negations: types/global.d.ts is hand-written and must stay tracked, and
# websocket-server/dist is a separate build's output. next-env.d.ts is deliberately NOT
# negated - Next regenerates it and it is already ignored above, so un-ignoring it here
# would just add untracked noise to every checkout.
*.d.ts
*.d.ts.map
!types/global.d.ts
!websocket-server/dist/index.d.ts

# Compiled JavaScript under the TypeScript source trees.
# Scoped to these two directories on purpose: a blanket *.js would swallow legitimate
# hand-written files like ecosystem.config.js, scripts/*.js and the api-server build.
# Nothing under database/ or lib/ is hand-written JavaScript, so anything appearing here
# is emitted output and must not be committed.
/database/**/*.js
/database/**/*.js.map
/lib/**/*.js
/lib/**/*.js.map

# Local setup notes and screenshots. Owner decision, 2 Sep 2026: never commit these.
# Reason: setup-help screenshots routinely capture credentials, connection strings and
# dashboard tokens, and an image cannot be reviewed by a diff. Keeping the whole folder
# out means nobody has to make that judgement per file.
/Verif_Setup_help/
